WEBVTT

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:15.780
Engagement sends promo emails to the customers who agreed to hear from you, picked from what they bought, and keeps a history of every conversation. It sends through your own Mailchimp account. In this video, you’ll set it up, pick an audience, and send a campaign.

00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:26.659
Mailchimp connects in Engagement, under Connection. Your System Admin pastes in a Mailchimp API key, and picks the audience your customers are added to.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:36.444
Set the name and address promos come from, on your own domain. Worklynq picks who gets each email, and Mailchimp sends it, and handles unsubscribes.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:45.113
Anyone who unsubscribes is marked in Worklynq too, and never gets a promo again. Check unsubscribes brings the latest across.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:52.628
Campaigns lists every promo: drafts, scheduled, and sent, with how many people got it, opened it, and clicked.

00:00:53.067 --> 00:01:00.491
Open a draft. Who gets it is picked from your customers: their status, the kind of customer, their tags, and what they bought, and when.

00:01:00.933 --> 00:01:07.952
It tells you how many will get it, and who’s left out and why. Promo emails only go to customers who agreed to get them.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:16.485
Below, write the subject and the email: a heading, your message, and a button. Your address and an unsubscribe link are always added.

00:01:16.933 --> 00:01:25.040
Send yourself a test first. Then click Send, and send it now, or schedule it. You can save the emails you send often as templates.

